    "created_at": "2023-04-21T18:45:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-04-21T18:45:46Z",
    "body": "Actually, I don't think this example is a problem already. When `hidePopover()` runs for popover1, the \"hide all popovers until\" algorithm won't find anything to close, because it's just popover1 at that point. Further down, it'll get to [step 5.1](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-popover-algorithm) which will fire the `beforetoggle` which opens popover 2, and that will call \"hide all popovers until\" popover 2 (at [step 7.2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#show-popover)), which will actually finish hiding popover 1. Then we will exit this recursion and get back to the original `beforetoggle` for popover1, which will hit step 5.2 and find the popover already closed. Right?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
