    "body": "\r\n\r\n> Actually, I don't think this example is a problem already. When `hidePopover()` runs for popover1, the \"hide all popovers until\" algorithm won't find anything to close, because it's just popover1 at that point. Further down, it'll get to [step 5.1](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-popover-algorithm) which will fire the `beforetoggle` which opens popover 2, and that will call \"hide all popovers until\" popover 2 (at [step 7.2](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#show-popover)), which will actually finish hiding popover 1.\r\n\r\nHmm, looks like we can't finish hiding popover1 here, for here it will call `hidePopover()` for popover1, and again it fires the `beforetoggle` which opens popover 2.\r\n",
